~ start
Percussion Spirit: An intruder? Your voice is weak... thin like the air!
Percussion Spirit: Like these empty bowls, you lack weight. You vibrate too fast!
Percussion Spirit: Without mass, there is no depth. Without gravity, there is no music.
Percussion Spirit: Make them heavy. Make them sing. Or leave!

Mélos: (Thinking) He’s talking about mass... 
Mélos: (Thinking) If the bowls are empty, they are light and vibrate too fast. That's why the sound is so high.
Mélos: (Thinking) I need to add water. More mass will slow the vibrations down and create a deep, low sound!

Percussion Spirit: Ok now it's your turn, I want you to play me a tune: low, high, low.
=> END